ICU (src/intl*.cpp, src/temporal_calendar.cpp)
----------------------------------------------

Intl (ECMA-402) uses ICU, International Components for Unicode
(https://icu.unicode.org/), through its C API: the system's ICU library (on
Windows, the ICU in Windows (icu.dll)), which is linked and not included in
neos. ICU's locale data (CLDR) and formatting provide Intl's locale
negotiation, collation, number, date, list, relative time, display name,
segmentation and duration formatting and Temporal's non-ISO 8601 calendars.
